  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening law endorcement for the protection of the Critically Endangered Sumatra orangutan in Singkil peat swamp forest, Aceh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Singkil Wildlife Sanctuary (a peat swamp forest) is home to the important Critically Endangered Sumatra orangutan. The Sanctuary has an extremely high conservation value because it contains one of the highest known orangutan densities (1.75 individuals/km2). Despite this, both for the Sumatra orangutan population and peat swamp, Singkil is currently under threat due to agricultural clearance for oil palm, fires and illegal logging. This proposal aims to address all of these threats by strengthening the law enforcement for protection of the orangutan population and its peat swamp habitat. This will be combined with awareness activities through assisting the communities around Singkil in mitigating human-wildlife conflict. The project has the following objectives: (1) Reducing forest encroachment, illegal logging, and other threats in key orangutan habitat in Singkil Wildlife Sanctuary; and, (2) Mitigating human wildlife conflict (particularly orangutan) around Singkil Wildlife Sanctuary and increasing awareness of the community on the importance of Singkil as orangutan habitat.</narrative>
  </description>
